{"study_accession":"PRJNA991973","secondary_study_accession":"SRP447809","title":"Stimulation of PSTPIP1 to trigger proinflammatory responses in asymptomatic SARS-CoV-2 infections","description":"A hyperinflammatory response to severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) infection gravely worsens the clinical progression of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19). Although the undesirable effects of inflammasome activation have been correlated to the severity of COVID-19, the mechanisms of this process in the asymptomatic infection and disease progression have not yet been clearly elucidated. Our results indicate potential preventive targets for COVID-19 disease development and progression. Overall design: We performed strand-specific RNA sequencing in 39 peripheral blood mononuclear cell (PBMC) samples from asymptomatic individuals, symptomatic patients and healthy donors.","pubmed":"38463809","geo_series":"","n_samples":39,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN36344751","study_accession":"PRJNA991973","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Homo sapiens, symptomatic individual, 16","description":"Homo sapiens, symptomatic individual, 16","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7567121","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-07-12","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood mononuclear cell"],["disease","symptomatic"],["cell_type","peripheral blood mononuclear cell"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR25180217","experiment_accession":"SRX20928174","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":34301911,"base_count":9562517552,"first_public":"2023-07-12","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7567121: Homo sapiens, symptomatic individual, 16 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN36344752","study_accession":"PRJNA991973","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Homo sapi